    "narrative": "For LawDog today, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.96) and **Bryce Harper** (72.70) anchor our lineup, both benefiting from high-leverage spots against left-handed starters. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is particularly enticing; his ability to exploit Valdez\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base potential, which is vital given our emphasis on the scarcity of that category. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (66.94) remains a primary play against Pfaadt; while the base projection is modest, the favorable platoon split and Pfaadt\u2019s generous allowance of stolen bases elevate **Daulton Varsho** into \"Strong\" territory. **Cal Raleigh** (74.07) also grades out elite today, as his power-first profile aligns perfectly with an exploitable matchup against Springs.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Braden Montgomery** (42.58). While he sits just above the floor, the combination of a tough matchup against Bradley and the higher efficiency of starters like **JJ Bleday** pushed him to the pine. We are keeping a close watch on **Jonathan Aranda** (50.72) and **Zack Gelof** (49.01), as their scores are dangerously close to the marginal threshold; both are facing tough arms in deGrom and Kirby, respectively. If we see any defensive shifts or lineup drops from the likes of **Tyler Freeman**, **Matt Chapman**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, or **Kyle Karros**, we will re-evaluate, but for now, the bench remains deep to preserve our daily game caps.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the early slate, specifically regarding the high-end talent facing elite arms. **Jonathan Aranda** faces the most significant hurdle against deGrom, whose 3.15 xERA demands caution, and the lack of official lineup confirmation for some auxiliary pieces necessitates a final check before first pitch. We are comfortable holding **Will Smith** and **Justin Crawford** in reserve, as their unavailability or lack of projected volume makes them non-factors for this rotation. Expect **Lawrence Butler** (61.72) to provide the necessary spark in the outfield if he can navigate the Kirby matchup, relying on his dynamic platoon edge to offset the park penalty.",
